{
  "count": 86,
  "cues": [
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-01",
      "start": 1.8,
      "end": 4.009291666666667,
      "text": "A heart is placed on a scale."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-02",
      "start": 4.309291666666667,
      "end": 9.877958333333334,
      "text": "On the other side sits a single feather,\nthe sign of Maat, truth and right order."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-03",
      "start": 10.177958333333335,
      "end": 14.524309210526317,
      "text": "People often say that the heart\nhad to be lighter than the feather,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-03",
      "start": 14.524309210526317,
      "end": 17.685291666666668,
      "text": "and that if it failed,\na monster would devour it."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-04",
      "start": 17.98529166666667,
      "end": 22.911291666666667,
      "text": "This is the famous Weighing of the Heart,\nfrom the Egyptian Book of the Dead."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-05",
      "start": 23.211291666666668,
      "end": 26.124583333333334,
      "text": "It sounds like a terrifying final exam."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P01-06",
      "start": 26.424583333333334,
      "end": 29.039208333333335,
      "text": "But what does the book\nitself actually say?"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P02-01",
      "start": 33.3,
      "end": 38.36733548109965,
      "text": "In this episode, we open the\nBook of the Dead itself: its real name,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P02-01",
      "start": 38.36733548109965,
      "end": 43.81283032646048,
      "text": "a list of wrongs never done, forty-two\ngods, a spell spoken to the heart,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P02-01",
      "start": 43.81283032646048,
      "end": 47.97258333333333,
      "text": "and the question of whether\nanyone was expected to fail."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P03-01",
      "start": 56.166666666666664,
      "end": 58.994625,
      "text": "First, there was no\nsingle Book of the Dead."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P03-02",
      "start": 59.294624999999996,
      "end": 63.80529166666666,
      "text": "These texts were known by phrases\nsuch as going forth by day."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P03-03",
      "start": 64.10529166666666,
      "end": 67.91154711838006,
      "text": "In the New Kingdom, selections\nof these spells came to be"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P03-03",
      "start": 67.91154711838006,
      "end": 71.37795833333332,
      "text": "written on papyrus scrolls\nand buried with the dead."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P03-04",
      "start": 71.67795833333334,
      "end": 75.85729166666667,
      "text": "The choice and order of spells\nvaried from scroll to scroll."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P03-05",
      "start": 76.15729166666667,
      "end": 81.20129166666666,
      "text": "On some, the owner's name was written\nin later, in spaces left blank."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P03-06",
      "start": 81.50129166666666,
      "end": 84.10591666666667,
      "text": "Some scrolls held only a few spells."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P03-07",
      "start": 84.40591666666666,
      "end": 87.23654166666667,
      "text": "Others held more than a hundred and fifty."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P04-01",
      "start": 89.4,
      "end": 91.918,
      "text": "The name Book of the Dead is modern."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P04-02",
      "start": 92.218,
      "end": 98.07128997289973,
      "text": "In 1842, the German scholar Karl\nRichard Lepsius published a long"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P04-02",
      "start": 98.07128997289973,
      "end": 103.46729166666667,
      "text": "papyrus kept in Turin, under\nthe title the Book of the Dead."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P04-03",
      "start": 103.76729166666667,
      "end": 106.76140411646587,
      "text": "His numbering of its spells\nbecame the basis"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P04-03",
      "start": 106.76140411646587,
      "end": 109.546625,
      "text": "of the numbers scholars still use today."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P04-04",
      "start": 109.846625,
      "end": 114.920625,
      "text": "The judgment we are looking\nfor is mainly in Spell 125."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P05-01",
      "start": 116.73333333333333,
      "end": 123.21533333333333,
      "text": "Spell 125 takes the dead person into\na great hall, the Hall of the Two Truths."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P05-02",
      "start": 123.51533333333333,
      "end": 126.53395833333333,
      "text": "There, the dead person\nspeaks for themselves."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P05-03",
      "start": 126.83395833333333,
      "end": 131.38729166666667,
      "text": "They greet the great god, the lord\nof truth, and say that they know him."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P05-04",
      "start": 131.68729166666668,
      "end": 134.15395833333332,
      "text": "Then they list the wrongs they never did."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P06-01",
      "start": 135.46666666666667,
      "end": 138.32729166666667,
      "text": "Scholars call this\nthe Negative Confession."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P06-02",
      "start": 138.62729166666668,
      "end": 140.89191666666667,
      "text": "Its lines are short and plain."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P06-03",
      "start": 141.19191666666666,
      "end": 145.95850000000002,
      "text": "Here are a few, from different versions,\nin an old English translation."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P06-04",
      "start": 146.2585,
      "end": 147.94579166666668,
      "text": "I have not stolen."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P06-05",
      "start": 148.24579166666666,
      "end": 150.06975,
      "text": "I have done no murder."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P06-06",
      "start": 150.36975,
      "end": 152.29041666666666,
      "text": "I have spoken no lies."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P06-07",
      "start": 152.59041666666667,
      "end": 154.606375,
      "text": "I have made no man to weep."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P06-08",
      "start": 154.906375,
      "end": 157.75566666666668,
      "text": "I have not turned back\nwater at its springtide."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P07-01",
      "start": 160.86666666666667,
      "end": 164.0411472868217,
      "text": "Then the dead person\nturns to forty-two gods,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P07-01",
      "start": 164.0411472868217,
      "end": 167.07133333333334,
      "text": "and greets each one by a name and a place."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P07-02",
      "start": 167.37133333333335,
      "end": 171.11868926553674,
      "text": "The first is greeted as the one\nwhose strides are long,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P07-02",
      "start": 171.11868926553674,
      "end": 175.56,
      "text": "who comes forth from Annu, the city\nthe Greeks called Heliopolis."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P07-03",
      "start": 175.86,
      "end": 180.57266666666666,
      "text": "To each god, the dead person names\none more wrong they did not do."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P07-04",
      "start": 180.87266666666667,
      "end": 182.72933333333333,
      "text": "Knowing the names mattered."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P07-05",
      "start": 183.02933333333334,
      "end": 186.72933333333333,
      "text": "One version ends, I know\nyou, and I know your names."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P08-01",
      "start": 194.2,
      "end": 196.47329166666665,
      "text": "But what if the heart disagreed?"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P08-02",
      "start": 196.77329166666667,
      "end": 201.10195833333333,
      "text": "For the Egyptians, the heart\nwas the center of thought and feeling."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P08-03",
      "start": 201.4019583333333,
      "end": 204.90995833333332,
      "text": "It was believed to remember\nwhat a person had done."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P08-04",
      "start": 205.20995833333333,
      "end": 209.592625,
      "text": "So another spell, Spell 30B,\nspeaks directly to the heart."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P08-05",
      "start": 209.89262499999998,
      "end": 213.88729166666667,
      "text": "In an old translation, it\nbegins, My heart my mother."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P08-06",
      "start": 214.18729166666665,
      "end": 218.07033082706766,
      "text": "It asks that nothing oppose\nthe dead person at the judgment,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P08-06",
      "start": 218.07033082706766,
      "end": 222.94058333333334,
      "text": "and that the heart not be parted\nfrom them before the keeper of the scales."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P08-07",
      "start": 223.24058333333332,
      "end": 228.59324999999998,
      "text": "Modern translators read it as a plea that\nthe heart not speak against its owner."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P09-01",
      "start": 234.73333333333332,
      "end": 239.821815647482,
      "text": "This spell was often inscribed\non a heart scarab, an amulet in the shape"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P09-01",
      "start": 239.821815647482,
      "end": 244.69529166666666,
      "text": "of a beetle, and such scarabs\nwere often placed on the mummy's chest."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P09-02",
      "start": 244.99529166666665,
      "end": 248.4641955128205,
      "text": "On this one, with a human head, the museum"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P09-02",
      "start": 248.4641955128205,
      "end": 252.51125,
      "text": "identifies the ten lines\non the base as Spell 30B."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P09-03",
      "start": 252.81124999999997,
      "end": 255.90654166666667,
      "text": "The dead person did not\nface the scale alone."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P09-04",
      "start": 256.2065416666667,
      "end": 258.6191666666667,
      "text": "They brought their own\nwords for the heart."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P10-01",
      "start": 261.3333333333333,
      "end": 263.340625,
      "text": "Now look again at the scale."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P10-02",
      "start": 263.640625,
      "end": 266.7785833333333,
      "text": "Here, the heart is not shown\nlighter than the feather."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P10-03",
      "start": 267.0785833333333,
      "end": 269.3405833333333,
      "text": "The two sides hang in balance."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P10-04",
      "start": 269.6405833333333,
      "end": 273.70191666666665,
      "text": "Museum descriptions speak\nof the heart balancing with Maat."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P10-05",
      "start": 274.00191666666666,
      "end": 276.09454166666666,
      "text": "Thoth writes down the result."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P10-06",
      "start": 276.39454166666667,
      "end": 279.22249999999997,
      "text": "And nearby waits Ammit, the Devourer."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P10-07",
      "start": 279.5225,
      "end": 283.02495238095236,
      "text": "One old description\ncalls her part crocodile,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P10-07",
      "start": 283.02495238095236,
      "end": 285.65179166666667,
      "text": "part lion, and part hippopotamus."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-01",
      "start": 287.8333333333333,
      "end": 290.9633333333333,
      "text": "But papyri made to help\nthe dead live on are"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-01",
      "start": 290.9633333333333,
      "end": 294.0933333333333,
      "text": "unlikely to show\ntheir owner being devoured."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-02",
      "start": 294.3933333333333,
      "end": 297.1990957854406,
      "text": "In the text, the heart is found true,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-02",
      "start": 297.1990957854406,
      "end": 300.99066666666664,
      "text": "and the dead person is allowed\nto go before Osiris."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-03",
      "start": 301.29066666666665,
      "end": 304.532625,
      "text": "The scroll was made to help\nsecure a good outcome."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P11-04",
      "start": 304.832625,
      "end": 308.99924999999996,
      "text": "After their names, the dead\nwere often called true of voice."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-01",
      "start": 314.3666666666667,
      "end": 317.15195833333337,
      "text": "So, could you fail\nthe Weighing of the Heart?"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-02",
      "start": 317.4519583333333,
      "end": 319.264625,
      "text": "As a fear, yes."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-03",
      "start": 319.56462500000004,
      "end": 321.570625,
      "text": "That is why Ammit is there."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-04",
      "start": 321.870625,
      "end": 325.2379583333333,
      "text": "But the Book of the Dead\nwas made to help you pass."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-05",
      "start": 325.53795833333334,
      "end": 329.01795833333335,
      "text": "And its denials also describe a good life:"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P12-05",
      "start": 329.01795833333335,
      "end": 333.07795833333336,
      "text": "do not steal, do not lie,\ndo not make others weep."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P13-01",
      "start": 338.46666666666664,
      "end": 340.7939583333333,
      "text": "Every story has an origin."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P13-02",
      "start": 341.0939583333333,
      "end": 344.2656020833333,
      "text": "Sometimes, it begins\nwith a heart, a feather,"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P13-02",
      "start": 344.2656020833333,
      "end": 346.8605833333333,
      "text": "and a few words prepared in advance."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P14-01",
      "start": 349.23333333333335,
      "end": 354.3926666666667,
      "text": "This video is based on historical\ntexts and public museum collections."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P14-02",
      "start": 354.6926666666667,
      "end": 357.412625,
      "text": "The narration uses synthetic speech."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P14-03",
      "start": 357.712625,
      "end": 361.668625,
      "text": "Sources and terms of use are\nlisted in the description."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P14-04",
      "start": 361.96862500000003,
      "end": 364.73749801587303,
      "text": "If you enjoyed this story, please like"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P14-04",
      "start": 364.73749801587303,
      "end": 368.08929166666667,
      "text": "the video and subscribe\nfor more quiet origins."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "P14-05",
      "start": 368.3892916666667,
      "end": 370.1619166666667,
      "text": "Thank you for watching."
    }
  ],
  "timing": "Exact synthesized sentence boundaries; within-sentence pages weighted by text length",
  "script_matches_ignoring_layout_whitespace": true
}
